{"titulo": "❌ “Operation failed”", "demo": "2.2", "dominio": 2, "simulada": false, "fecha": "2026-11-23 12:53", "ajustes": {"D22_FORMATO": "generico", "DETALLE": "basico"}, "lineas": ["🎛  Panel settings for this run: D22_FORMATO = \"generico\"", "\u001b[2m   Model: claude-haiku-\u001b[0m\u001b[1;2;36m5\u001b[0m\u001b[2m-\u001b[0m\u001b[1;2;36m5\u001b[0m", "\u001b[2m   HTML mode: on → salidas_html/dominio2/\u001b[0m", "", "\u001b[34m───────────────── \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37;48;5;18m DEMO \u001b[0m\u001b[1;37;48;5;18m2.2\u001b[0m\u001b[1;37;48;5;18m · Structured errors: so Claude knows WHAT failed and WHAT to do \u001b[0m\u001b[34m ─────────────────\u001b[0m", "", "\u001b[2m📖 This demo's guide: python lab_dominio2.py guia \u001b[0m\u001b[1;2;36m2.2\u001b[0m\u001b[2m  ·  more detail: set DETALLE = \u001b[0m\u001b[2;32m\"completo\"\u001b[0m\u001b[2m at the top of \u001b[0m", "\u001b[2mthe file\u001b[0m", "\u001b[33m╭─\u001b[0m\u001b[33m────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m 💡 Exam concept \u001b[0m\u001b[33m─────────────────────────────────────────────\u001b[0m\u001b[33m─╮\u001b[0m", "\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m                                                                                                            \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m", "\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m  A generic error ('Operation failed') doesn't tell Claude whether to retry, ask for other data or          \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m", "\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m  escalate. Worse: returning an empty list when the system failed makes Claude say something FALSE ('you    \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m", "\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m  have no orders').                                                                                         \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m", "\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m  Structured error = is_error: true + errorCategory (transient / validation / business / permission) +      \u001b[33m│\u001b[0m", "\u001b[33m│\u001b[0m  isRetryable + a readable description. And a valid empty result is NOT an error.                   